The union includes all unique elements from both sets.
```python
A = {1, 2, 3}
B = {3, 4, 5}
union_set = A.union(B) # or A | B
# union_set will be {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}
```

The intersection contains elements common to both sets.
```python
S1 = {'apple', 'banana', 'cherry'}
S2 = {'banana', 'grape', 'cherry'}
intersection_set = S1.intersection(S2) # or S1 & S2
# intersection_set will be {'banana', 'cherry'}
```

The difference $X - Y$ (or `X.difference(Y)`) contains elements present in $X$ that are not present in $Y$.
```python
X = {10, 20, 30, 40}
Y = {30, 40, 50}
difference_set = X.difference(Y) # or X - Y
# difference_set will be {10, 20}
```
